{ Welcome to my third study.
This is a try and a reflexion on the OPENING.

What does it mean "to know" an opening ?
At what point can we consider ourselves novice / regular / expert in our opening ?

In order to shed some light on the issue, I've identified 10 levels of mastery :

Level 1 : first moves
Level 2 : the philosophy
Level 3 : some basic theory
Level 4 : thematic tactics
Level 5 : thematic ideas
Level 6 : some advanced theory
Level 7 : some model games
Level 8 : tricks and traps
Level 9 : typical endgame
Level 10 : some expert theory

Please, keep in mind I've chosen the Dragon sicilian to illustrate my point but my real goal is to help you to identify your own level of mastery in your own opening, and what you can do to improve your knowledge. }
 *

