{ Level 1 : first moves
Well, you gotta start somewhere ! }
1. e4 c5 { Sicilian defense } 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 { White chooses the open sicilian, this leads us to the famous "Sicilian Labyrinth", considering the numerous variants and transpositions that may occur. } 3... cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 { And we enter the "Dragon" territory. The sicilian dragon is the opening I've chosen to illustrate my point because I've been playing and studying it for quite a time, but please keep in mind that I'm speaking about the opening in general. } *

