{ Level 2 : the philosophy
I'm trully convinced we are doing better when we enjoy what we do. I would even say you have to be one with the spirit of your opening !

This is a typical double-edge opposite castling dragon position. This is not for the faint-hearted and it will end most likely in a blood bath (or into fire if you want to stick in the dragon theme). A true dragon player should embrace such type of position.

When you're looking for an opening, you must get to know its philosophy, its essence. And you must also know what you're looking for, what suits you well.
Do you want a close and quiet position ? Do you want a tactical fight ? Do you prefer to have the space or do you prefer to let it and counter-attack it ?

Also, I really recommend you not to lock yourself into a single playstyle, but to explore what chess has to offer. In the long run, you really benefit from the knowledge of different pawn structures, different approaches... }
 *

