{ Level 3 : some basic theory }
1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 { White is preparing the very dangerous and very famous Yougoslav attack ! } 6... Bg7 7. f3 O-O 8. Qd2 { White plan is to long castle, and after that go for a direct attack on black king thanks to h4-h5 looking for the lever / hook on h5 (ref : the weapon every player should master https://lichess.org/study/7KLT2c9k). If black plays h5 itself, then the lever / hook is now on g4 !
This attack was a favorite from Bobby Fischer } 8... Nc6 9. Bc4 { To understand a little subtlety about Bc4, please wait for the two next chapters } 9... Bd7 10. O-O-O Rc8 { Threatening Nxd4 } 11. Bb3 (11. h4?? Nxd4 12. Qxd4 Ng4! 13. Qd3 { The queen is overloaded } 13... Nxe3 14. Qxe3 Rxc4 $19) 11... Ne5 { And we reach a typical double edge dragon position, where black has some Nc4 coming to start the counter-attack. } 12. Kb1 Nc4 13. Bxc4 Rxc4 { White has given his light square bishop because the Be3 is more valuable. Now the party can get started... } *

