1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 { White is preparing the very dangerous and very famous Yougoslav attack ! } 6... Bg7 7. f3 O-O 8. Qd2 { White plan is to long castle, and after that go for a direct attack on black king thanks to h4-h5 looking for the lever / hook on h5 (ref : the weapon every player should master https://lichess.org/study/7KLT2c9k). If black plays h5 itself, then the lever / hook is now on g4 !
This attack was a favorite from Bobby Fischer } 8... Nc6 9. O-O-O { Now let's see what happens if black goes for the same plan than in previous chapter : } 9... Bd7 10. Kb1 Rc8 11. g4 Ne5 12. h4 Nc4 13. Bxc4 Rxc4 14. h5 $18 { Black position is about to collapse while the counter-attack has not even started yet. The reason is simple : white has saved the moves Bc4 and Bb3, capturing the Nc4 from f1 instead of b3 ! Two tempos (or tempis) in such critical positions can change the outcome of the game. } *

