15... fxe5! 16. fxe5 (16. Bxf8 Qxf8 17. fxe5?? Bh6 $19) 16... Bxe5! 17. Bxf8 Qxf8 { Another typical exchange sac, this time on f8. As a result, Black has an absolute control over the black squares and the pieces come very quickly into the attack (Rb8, Qf8 to a3 or b4).
We also have that good little bonus (e5 pawn) to get full compensation for the exchange. } 18. Kb1 Rb8 19. b3 (19. c3 Qa3! { Threatening Bc3 } 20. Rc1 (20. Ka1 Rxb2! 21. Qxb2 Bxc3 $19) (20. Kc1 Qxa2 $19) 20... Bf4! $19) 19... Qa3 20. Qc1 (20. c3 Rxb3+ 21. axb3 Qxb3+ 22. Kc1 (22. Qb2 Qxd1+ $19) 22... Bxc3 23. Qc2 Qa3+ 24. Kb1 Qa1#) 20... Qc5 { Threatening Qc3 } 21. c4 (21. Rd3 Bg7! { e5 to come with Bf5, e4 etc. }) 21... Qa5 { With some cute mating threats } 22. Qe3 (22. h4 Rxb3+ 23. axb3 Qa1+ 24. Kc2 Qc3+ 25. Kb1 Qxb3+ 26. Qb2 Qxb2#) 22... Bc3 23. h4 (23. Rd3 Bg7 $19 { You don't wanna be White here, just look at the black squares }) 23... Rxb3+! 24. axb3 Qa1+ 25. Kc2 Qb2+ 26. Kd3 e5! $19 *

