{ Level 7 : some advanced theory
I know this is scary but please remember the higher your elo is, the higher your knowledge should be. You don't need to remember 15 moves in every lines if you're around 1500 elo for example ! (don't take it personally, even Magnus had 1500 elo at one point (well he was 3 yo)) }
1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 g6 6. Be3 Bg7 7. f3 O-O 8. Qd2 Nc6 9. Bc4 Bd7 10. O-O-O Rc8 11. Bb3 Ne5 12. Bh6 { The caveman approach, aiming for the most straight forward attack possible. Next moves h4-h5-checkmate ! } 12... Bxh6 13. Qxh6 Rxc3! { Attack : counter-attack !
Pro tip : when the queen is far, the exchange sac becomes even more dangerous } 14. bxc3 Qc7 15. Kb2 { Bad but this is simply the most played move on Internet. Defends the c3 pawn and remove the king from the C-file. } 15... Rc8 16. Qd2 a5 { Threaten to win the bishop with a4 } 17. a4 Bxa4! 18. Ra1 (18. Bxa4 Nc4+ $19) 18... Bd7 19. h4 a4! $19 { And here we go again ! This is how you deal with the caveman line, just by being even more cavemaner than him } *

